    ],
    "configuration": {
      "title": "Better Worktrees",
      "properties": {
        "betterWorktrees.showNotifications": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "description": "Show success notifications. Warnings and errors are always shown."
        },
        "betterWorktrees.openWorktreeIn": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "newWindow",
            "currentWindow"
          ],
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Open the worktree in a new window.",
            "Open the worktree in the current window, replacing the current folder."
          ],
          "default": "newWindow",
          "markdownDescription": "Default target for `Open Worktree...` and the worktree open actions. Clicking a worktree row narrows the Source Control view to that worktree instead; use `Show All Worktrees in Source Control` to restore the others."
        },
        "betterWorktrees.scanDepth": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 3,
          "minimum": 0,
          "markdownDescription": "How many directory levels deep to search each workspace folder for git repositories. `0` scans only the workspace folder root; higher values discover repos nested inside it. Directories such as `node_modules`, `dist`, and `.venv` are always skipped."
        },
        "betterWorktrees.worktreePathTemplate": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "${repoPath}/../${repoName}-${branch}",
          "markdownDescription": "Where `New Worktree...` suggests putting a new worktree. The suggestion is always shown and can be edited before anything is created.\n\nPlaceholders: `${repoPath}` (absolute path of the repository), `${repoName}` (its directory name), and `${branch}` (the new branch, with slashes flattened to hyphens so it stays a single directory). A leading `~` expands to your home directory, and a relative path resolves against the repository.\n\nFor example, `~/.worktrees/${repoName}/${branch}` collects every worktree under one directory."
        },
        "betterWorktrees.colorMode": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "branch",
            "branchType"
          ],
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Give each branch its own stable colour, hashed from the branch name. Different branches are easy to tell apart.",
            "Colour by branch type (feature, fix, release, ...). All branches of the same type share a colour, so you scan by category."
          ],
          "default": "branch",
          "markdownDescription": "How worktree folders are coloured in the Explorer.\n\n- `branch` — each branch gets a distinct hashed colour from a 20-colour palette (`betterWorktrees.worktreeColor1`–`20`).\n- `branchType` — colour by the branch's type mapped through `#betterWorktrees.branchTypeMap#`, using the `betterWorktrees.worktreeType*` colours.\n\nAll colours are themeable via `workbench.colorCustomizations`."
        },
        "betterWorktrees.sortDirtyFirst": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "Sort worktrees with uncommitted changes ahead of clean ones (after the current window's worktree). Toggle it from the view title. When off, worktrees are ordered alphabetically."
        },
        "betterWorktrees.branchTypeMap": {
          "type": "object",
          "scope": "resource",
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "main",
              "feature",
              "fix",
              "release",
              "chore",
              "other"
            ]
          },
          "default": {},
          "markdownDescription": "Overrides for the branch-keyword → type mapping used when `#betterWorktrees.colorMode#` is `branchType`. Each key is a token that may appear anywhere in a branch name (branches are split on `/`, `-`, `_`, and `.`), matched case-insensitively; each value is one of `main`, `feature`, `fix`, `release`, `chore`, `other`.\n\nBecause every token is matched, `user/login-crash-fix` is detected as a **fix** even though `fix` is not the leading segment. When several types match, precedence is `fix` > `release` > `feature` > `chore` > `main`.\n\nEntries here are merged over the built-in defaults (`main`/`master`/`develop`/`trunk` → main, `feat`/`feature` → feature, `fix`/`bugfix`/`hotfix`/`bug`/`patch` → fix, `release`/`rel`/`rc` → release, `chore`/`refactor`/`docs`/`test`/`ci`/`build`/`deps`/`style`/`perf` → chore). For example `{ \"wip\": \"chore\", \"epic\": \"feature\" }` adds two keywords without removing the defaults.\n\nEach type maps to a themeable colour: `betterWorktrees.worktreeTypeMain`, `...Feature`, `...Fix`, `...Release`, `...Chore`, `...Other`."
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "scripts": {
    "vscode:prepublish": "npm run clean && npm run compile",
    "clean": "rm -rf out",
    "compile": "tsc -p ./",
    "watch": "tsc -watch -p ./",
    "test": "vitest run",
    "lint": "eslint src --ext ts",
    "package": "npx @vscode/vsce package --no-dependencies"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@types/node": "^20.11.0",
    "@types/vscode": "^1.85.0",
    "@vscode/vsce": "2.22.0",
    "eslint": "^10.6.0",
    "typescript": "^5.3.0",
    "typescript-eslint": "^8.62.1",
    "vitest": "^4.1.9"
  }
}
